d generative models? — discriminative P(y|x) vs generative P(x)/P(x,y), BERT vs GPT contrast, autoregressive vs diffusion taxonomy, hallucination risk as production consequence\n20\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-016: What is graph RAG? How does it differ from standard RAG? — knowledge graph construction (entity extraction, Neo4j/Kuzu), local vs global search (community summaries), multi-hop retrieval, tradeoff table vs standard RAG, Microsoft GraphRAG 2024 benchmark\n21\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-017: What is reflection in the context of LLM agents? — generate→critique→revise loop, Reflexion episodic memory, tool-feedback vs introspective reflection, HumanEval 67%→88% benchmark, conditional triggering for production cost control\n22\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-018: Explain KL divergence — formula, asymmetry (forward/reverse KL), RLHF PPO KL leash (β term), DPO closed-form derivation, reward hacking connection, cross-entropy relationship\n23\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-019: What is the difference between symbolic and connectionist AI? — GOFAI vs connectionist paradigms, MYCIN vs LLM contrast, neurosymbolic hybrids (tool-use agents, o1 scratchpad), interpretability tradeoff in regulated domains\n24\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-020: Describe text summarization techniques — extractive (TextRank), abstractive (Map-Reduce/Refine patterns, LangChain), query-focused, faithfulness gating with RAGAS, cost tiering for map vs reduce steps\n25\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 01-021: How do you do memory management and context management with LLMs? — four-tier memory architecture (in-context sliding window, vector store semantic memory, summarization layer, structured DB for exact facts), prompt compression (LLMLingua), LangChain ConversationSummaryBufferMemory, production cost/latency tradeoffs\n26\t2026-06-16 | 01-llm-fundamentals | wrote answer 